B.SI=new A.jF("Teck Valley India Pvt Ltd","Sr. Software Engineer (Flutter)","01/2022 - Present","At Teck Valley India, My current terminal, I have evolved into a Senior Software Engineer, partnering with clients across diverse industries to transform ideas into production-ready mobile solutions. My work spans full-scale product development, technical research, Proof of Concepts (PoCs), and Minimum Viable Products (MVPs), helping businesses validate ideas and accelerate innovation.\n\nOver the years, I have designed and architected cross-platform applications using Flutter while working on a wide range of technologies, including IoT and BLE-enabled devices, AI-powered business solutions, face recognition, enterprise software, and real-time communication systems. Alongside client projects, I continuously explore emerging AI and Machine Learning technologies by building and integrating custom models into mobile applications for both online and offline use, driven by a passion for continuous learning and technical innovation.",!0,!1)
B.SM=new A.jF("Tweaking Technologies","Android Developer","05/2019 - 01/2022","At Tweaking Technologies, I developed engaging educational and productivity applications for Android, including interactive learning games such as ABCD Drawing and Math Games that combined multiple activities into a single experience for children. During this time, I also began my journey with Flutter by developing Brain Game, an application focused on enhancing memory, concentration, and critical thinking. This role marked my transition from native Android development to cross-platform mobile development while expanding my expertise in UI/UX, game logic, and application architecture.",!1,!1)
B.SK=new A.jF("Systweak Software","Android Developer","05/2015 - 08/2017","At Systweak Software, I deepened my expertise in Android by developing high-performance utility applications that interacted closely with the Android operating system. I worked on products including Photos Cleaner, Instagram and Snapchat Lockers, memory optimization, storage management, and system utility applications. This role provided hands-on experience with Android internals, background services, accessibility APIs, storage management, system events, permissions, and performance optimization, strengthening my understanding of the Android platform beyond traditional application development.",!1,!1)
B.SH=new A.jF("Pegasus Technologies","Sr. Android Developer","09/2013 - 04/2015","At Pegasus Technologies, I transitioned from a trainee to a professional Android Developer, contributing to the development of enterprise mobility solutions for the hospitality industry. I worked on a comprehensive restaurant and hotel management platform that streamlined dine-in reservations, table ordering through handheld tablets, kitchen operations, home delivery, drive-through services, live driver tracking, and payment management. This experience strengthened my skills in building scalable, real-world enterprise applications and collaborating across multiple interconnected mobile solutions.",!1,!1)
B.SL=new A.jF("RRSC / ISRO \u2013 Jodhpur","Android Trainee","2012 - 2013","Joined RRSC/ISRO as an Android Trainee, where I learned Android application development and built my first production-style mobile application for farmers. The application enabled farm boundary mapping, land area calculation, geotagging, and soil sample data collection, introducing me to GIS-based mobile solutions and laying the foundation for my career in mobile development.",!1,!1)
B.SJ=new A.jF("Samarth BCA College","Lecturer (C & Networks)","2010 - 2011","Started my professional journey as a Lecturer, teaching C Programming and Network Technologies to undergraduate students. This role strengthened my technical fundamentals, communication skills, and ability to simplify complex concepts\u2014laying the foundation for my transition into software development.",!1,!0)
